IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc5-s117-02-to-117-06.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART III, the sub-heading "Search and Seizure" (sections 117.02 to 117.06). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Provisions addressed to a peace officer or a justice are encoded for what they decide about the person searched or the person whose things are seized.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING) or a core type. JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING otherwise.

§ `Part III continued -- search and seizure (ss 117.02 to 117.06)`

§§ `s 117.02 Search and seizure without warrant where offence committed`

-- src:2563 | 117.02 (1) Where a peace officer believes on reasonable grounds
-- src:2564 | (a) that a weapon, an imitation firearm, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance was used in the commission of an offence, or
-- src:2565 | (b) that an offence is being committed, or has been committed, under any provision of this Act that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, an imitation firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance,
-- src:2566 | and evidence of the offence is likely to be found on a person, in a vehicle or in any place or premises other than a dwelling-house, the peace officer may, where the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist but, by reason of exigent circumstances, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant, search, without warrant, the person, vehicle, place or premises, and seize any thing by means of or in relation to which that peace officer believes on reasonable grounds the offence is being committed or has been committed.
@ref s 117.02(1) (src:2563-2566)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the officer is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that a weapon, an imitation firearm, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance was used in the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that an offence is being committed, or has been committed, under a provision of this Act that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, an imitation firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that evidence of the offence is likely to be found on a person, in a vehicle or in a place or premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 dwelling-house: the place or premises is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of exigent circumstances, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.02(1) the peace officer may search without a warrant and seize` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 2 peace officer: the officer is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that a weapon, an imitation firearm, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance was used in the commission of an offence` OR `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that an offence is being committed, or has been committed, under a provision of this Act that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, an imitation firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance`) AND `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that evidence of the offence is likely to be found on a person, in a vehicle or in a place or premises` AND (`s 2 dwelling-house: the place or premises is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND `the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist` AND `by reason of exigent circumstances, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a peace officer believes on reasonable grounds"

-- src:2568 | (2) Any thing seized pursuant to subsection (1) shall be dealt with in accordance with sections 490 and 491.
@ref s 117.02(2) (src:2568)
GIVEN `the thing is seized pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.02(2) the thing seized is to be dealt with in accordance with sections 490 and 491` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is seized pursuant to subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 117.03 Seizure on failure to produce authorization`

-- src:2570 | 117.03 (1) Despite section 117.02, a peace officer who finds
-- src:2571 | (a) a person in possession of a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm who fails, on demand, to produce, for inspection by the peace officer, an authorization or a licence under which the person may lawfully possess the firearm and, in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, a registration certificate for it, or
-- src:2572 | (b) a person in possession of a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition who fails, on demand, to produce, for inspection by the peace officer, an authorization or a licence under which the person may lawfully possess it,
-- src:2573 | may seize the firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition unless its possession by the person in the circumstances in which it is found is authorized by any provision of this Part, or the person is under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who may lawfully possess it.
@ref s 117.03(1) (src:2570-2573)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the officer is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer finds a person in possession of a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm who fails, on demand, to produce, for inspection by the peace officer, an authorization or a licence under which the person may lawfully possess the firearm and, in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, a registration certificate for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer finds a person in possession of a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition who fails, on demand, to produce, for inspection by the peace officer, an authorization or a licence under which the person may lawfully possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its possession by the person in the circumstances in which it is found is authorized by any provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who may lawfully possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.03(1) the peace officer may seize the firearm, weapon, device or ammunition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `its possession by the person in the circumstances in which it is found is authorized by any provision of this Part` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless its possession by the person in the circumstances in which it is found is authorized by any provision of this Part"
        IF `the person is under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who may lawfully possess it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or the person is under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who may lawfully possess it"
        IF (`s 2 peace officer: the officer is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the peace officer finds a person in possession of a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm who fails, on demand, to produce, for inspection by the peace officer, an authorization or a licence under which the person may lawfully possess the firearm and, in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, a registration certificate for it` OR `the peace officer finds a person in possession of a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition who fails, on demand, to produce, for inspection by the peace officer, an authorization or a licence under which the person may lawfully possess it`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)


-- src:2575 | (2) If a person from whom any thing is seized under subsection (1) claims the thing within 14 days after the seizure and produces for inspection by the peace officer by whom it was seized, or any other peace officer having custody of it,
@ref s 117.03(2) (src:2575)
GIVEN `the date of the seizure` IS A DATE
      `the date of the claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.03(2) the claim is made within 14 days after the seizure` MEANS
    IF `the date of the claim` AT LEAST `the date of the seizure` AND `the date of the claim` AT MOST `the date of the seizure` PLUS 14
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "claims the thing within 14 days after the seizure"

-- src:2575 | (2) If a person from whom any thing is seized under subsection (1) claims the thing within 14 days after the seizure and produces for inspection by the peace officer by whom it was seized, or any other peace officer having custody of it,
-- src:2576 | (a) a licence under which the person is lawfully entitled to possess it, and
-- src:2577 | (b) in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, an authorization and registration certificate for it,
-- src:2578 | the thing shall without delay be returned to that person.
@ref s 117.03(2) (src:2575-2578)
GIVEN `the thing was seized from the person under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.03(2) the claim is made within 14 days after the seizure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person produces for inspection by the peace officer who seized it, or any other peace officer having custody of it, a licence under which the person is lawfully entitled to possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person produces an authorization and registration certificate for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.03(2) the thing is to be returned without delay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing was seized from the person under subsection (1)` AND (`the answer of s 117.03(2) the claim is made within 14 days after the seizure` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person produces for inspection by the peace officer who seized it, or any other peace officer having custody of it, a licence under which the person is lawfully entitled to possess it` AND ((NOT `the thing is a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm`) OR `the person produces an authorization and registration certificate for it`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person from whom any thing is seized under subsection (1) claims the thing within 14 days after the seizure and produces"


-- src:2575 | (2) If a person from whom any thing is seized under subsection (1) claims the thing within 14 days after the seizure and produces for inspection by the peace officer by whom it was seized, or any other peace officer having custody of it,
-- src:2578 | the thing shall without delay be returned to that person.
@ref s 117.03(2) (src:2575-2578)
DECLARE `s 117.03(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 117.03(2) claim the thing and produce the licence`
    `s 117.03(2) return the thing to the person`

@ref s 117.03(2) (src:2575-2578)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 117.03(2) act`
`s 117.03(2) the person may claim the thing within 14 days and the officer must then return it` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    DO `s 117.03(2) claim the thing and produce the licence`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE (
        PARTY `a peace officer`
        MUST `s 117.03(2) return the thing to the person`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `a peace officer` BECAUSE "the thing was not returned without delay")
    LEST FULFILLED

-- src:2580 | (3) Where any thing seized pursuant to subsection (1) is not claimed and returned as and when provided by subsection (2), a peace officer shall forthwith take the thing before a provincial court judge, who may, after affording the person from whom it was seized or its owner, if known, an opportunity to establish that the person is lawfully entitled to possess it, declare it to be forfeited to Her Majesty, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs.
@ref s 117.03(3) (src:2580)
GIVEN `the thing was seized pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing was claimed and returned as and when provided by subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.03(3) the peace officer is bound to take the thing forthwith before a provincial court judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing was seized pursuant to subsection (1)` AND (NOT `the thing was claimed and returned as and when provided by subsection (2)`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any thing seized pursuant to subsection (1) is not claimed and returned as and when provided by subsection (2)"

-- src:2580 | (3) Where any thing seized pursuant to subsection (1) is not claimed and returned as and when provided by subsection (2), a peace officer shall forthwith take the thing before a provincial court judge, who may, after affording the person from whom it was seized or its owner, if known, an opportunity to establish that the person is lawfully entitled to possess it, declare it to be forfeited to Her Majesty, to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs.
@ref s 117.03(3) (src:2580)
GIVEN `the thing was taken before the judge under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge has afforded the person from whom it was seized, or its owner if known, an opportunity to establish that the person is lawfully entitled to possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.03(3) the provincial court judge may declare the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing was taken before the judge under this subsection` AND `the judge has afforded the person from whom it was seized, or its owner if known, an opportunity to establish that the person is lawfully entitled to possess it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any thing seized pursuant to subsection (1) is not claimed and returned as and when provided by subsection (2), a peace officer shall forthwith take the thing before a provincial court judge, who may, after affording the person from whom it was seized or its owner, if known, an opportunity to establish that the person is lawfully entitled to possess it"

§§ `s 117.04 Application for warrant to search and seize`

-- src:2582 | 117.04 (1) Where, pursuant to an application made by a peace officer with respect to any person, a justice is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person possesses a weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance in a building, receptacle or place and that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess the weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search the building, receptacle or place and seize any such thing, and any authorization, licence or registration certificate relating to any such thing, that is held by or in the possession of the person.
@ref s 117.04(1) (src:2582)
GIVEN `s 2 justice: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a peace officer has applied with respect to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person possesses a weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance in a building, receptacle or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.04(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search the building, receptacle or place and seize` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 2 justice: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `a peace officer has applied with respect to the person` AND `the justice is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person possesses a weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance in a building, receptacle or place` AND `the justice is satisfied that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, pursuant to an application made by a peace officer with respect to any person, a justice is satisfied"

-- src:2584 | (2) Where, with respect to any person, a peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or any other person, for the person to possess any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, the peace officer may, where the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (1) exist but, by reason of a possible danger to the safety of that person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant, search for and seize any such thing, and any authorization, licence or registration certificate relating to any such thing, that is held by or in the possession of the person.
@ref s 117.04(2) (src:2584)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the officer is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or any other person, for the person to possess any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (1) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of a possible danger to the safety of that person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.04(2) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 2 peace officer: the officer is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or any other person, for the person to possess any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance` AND `the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (1) exist` AND `by reason of a possible danger to the safety of that person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, with respect to any person, a peace officer is satisfied"

-- src:2586 | (3) A peace officer who executes a warrant referred to in subsection (1) or who conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (2) shall immediately make a report to a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued, showing
@ref s 117.04(3) (src:2586)
GIVEN `the peace officer executes a warrant referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.04(3) the peace officer is bound to make a report immediately to a justice having jurisdiction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the peace officer executes a warrant referred to in subsection (1)` OR `the peace officer conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (2)`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2586 | (3) A peace officer who executes a warrant referred to in subsection (1) or who conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (2) shall immediately make a report to a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued, showing
-- src:2587 | (a) in the case of an execution of a warrant, the things or documents, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant; and
-- src:2588 | (b) in the case of a search conducted without a warrant, the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things or documents, if any, seized.
@ref s 117.04(3) (src:2586-2588)
GIVEN `the report is of an execution of a warrant and shows the things or documents, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is of a search without a warrant and shows the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things or documents, if any, seized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.04(3) the report shows what the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the report is of an execution of a warrant and shows the things or documents, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant` OR `the report is of a search without a warrant and shows the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things or documents, if any, seized`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2590 | (4) Where a peace officer who seizes any thing under subsection (1) or (2) is unable at the time of the seizure to seize an authorization or a licence under which the person from whom the thing was seized may possess the thing and, in the case of a seized firearm, a registration certificate for the firearm, every authorization, licence and registration certificate held by the person is, as at the time of the seizure, revoked.
@ref s 117.04(4) (src:2590)
GIVEN `a peace officer seizes any thing under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is unable at the time of the seizure to seize an authorization or a licence under which the person may possess the thing and, in the case of a seized firearm, a registration certificate for the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.04(4) every authorization, licence and registration certificate held by the person is revoked as at the time of the seizure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a peace officer seizes any thing under subsection (1) or (2)` AND `the peace officer is unable at the time of the seizure to seize an authorization or a licence under which the person may possess the thing and, in the case of a seized firearm, a registration certificate for the firearm` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a peace officer who seizes any thing under subsection (1) or (2) is unable at the time of the seizure"

§§ `s 117.05 Application for disposition`


-- src:2592 | 117.05 (1) If any thing or document has been seized under subsection 117.04(1) or (2), a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued shall, on application for an order for the disposition of the thing or document so seized made by a peace officer within 30 days after the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant, as the case may be, fix a date for the hearing of the application and direct that notice of the hearing be given to the persons or in the manner that the justice may specify.
@ref s 117.05(1) (src:2592)
GIVEN `the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application for an order for the disposition` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(1) the application is made within 30 days after the execution or the seizure` MEANS
    IF `the date of the application for an order for the disposition` AT LEAST `the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant`
       AND `the date of the application for an order for the disposition` AT MOST `the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant` PLUS 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant"

-- src:2592 | 117.05 (1) If any thing or document has been seized under subsection 117.04(1) or (2), a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued shall, on application for an order for the disposition of the thing or document so seized made by a peace officer within 30 days after the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant, as the case may be, fix a date for the hearing of the application and direct that notice of the hearing be given to the persons or in the manner that the justice may specify.
@ref s 117.05(1) (src:2592)
GIVEN `a thing or document has been seized under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application for an order for the disposition is made by a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.05(1) the application is made within 30 days after the execution or the seizure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(1) the justice is bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice of it be given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a thing or document has been seized under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` AND `the application for an order for the disposition is made by a peace officer` AND (`the answer of s 117.05(1) the application is made within 30 days after the execution or the seizure` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any thing or document has been seized under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)"


-- src:2592 | 117.05 (1) If any thing or document has been seized under subsection 117.04(1) or (2), a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued shall, on application for an order for the disposition of the thing or document so seized made by a peace officer within 30 days after the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant, as the case may be, fix a date for the hearing of the application and direct that notice of the hearing be given to the persons or in the manner that the justice may specify.
@ref s 117.05(1) (src:2592)
DECLARE `s 117.05(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 117.05(1) apply for an order for the disposition of the thing or document`
    `s 117.05(1) fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice be given`

@ref s 117.05(1) (src:2592)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 117.05(1) act`
`s 117.05(1) the peace officer may apply within 30 days and the justice must then fix a date for the hearing` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    DO `s 117.05(1) apply for an order for the disposition of the thing or document`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE (
        PARTY `a justice`
        MUST `s 117.05(1) fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice be given`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `a justice` BECAUSE "no date was fixed for the hearing")
    LEST FULFILLED

-- src:2594 | (2) A justice may proceed ex parte to hear and determine an application made under subsection (1) in the absence of the person from whom the thing or document was seized in the same circumstances as those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant.
@ref s 117.05(2) (src:2594)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person from whom the thing or document was seized is absent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part XXVII the circumstances are those in which a summary conviction court may proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(2) the justice may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is made under subsection (1)` AND `the person from whom the thing or document was seized is absent` AND (`Part XXVII the circumstances are those in which a summary conviction court may proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2596 | (3) At the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the justice shall hear all relevant evidence, including evidence respecting the value of the thing in respect of which the application was made.
@ref s 117.05(3) (src:2596)
GIVEN `the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) is held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(3) the justice is bound to hear all relevant evidence, including evidence respecting the value of the thing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) is held` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2598 | (4) If, following the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the justice finds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person from whom the thing was seized or of any other person that the person should possess any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance, or any such thing, the justice shall
-- src:2599 | (a) order that any thing seized be forfeited to Her Majesty or be otherwise disposed of; and
@ref s 117.05(4)(a) (src:2598-2599)
GIVEN `following the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the justice finds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person from whom the thing was seized or of any other person that the person should possess any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance, or any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(4)(a) the justice is bound to order that any thing seized be forfeited to Her Majesty or otherwise disposed of` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `following the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the justice finds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person from whom the thing was seized or of any other person that the person should possess any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance, or any such thing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, following the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the justice finds"

-- src:2598 | (4) If, following the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the justice finds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person from whom the thing was seized or of any other person that the person should possess any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance, or any such thing, the justice shall
-- src:2600 | (b) where the justice is satisfied that the circumstances warrant such an action, order that the possession by that person of any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance, or of any such thing, be prohibited during any period, not exceeding five years, that is specified in the order, beginning on the making of the order.
@ref s 117.05(4)(b) (src:2598-2600)
GIVEN `following the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the justice finds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person from whom the thing was seized or of any other person that the person should possess any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance, or any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied that the circumstances warrant such an action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(4)(b) the justice is bound to order that the person's possession be prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `following the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the justice finds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person from whom the thing was seized or of any other person that the person should possess any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance, or any such thing` AND `the justice is satisfied that the circumstances warrant such an action` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the justice is satisfied that the circumstances warrant such an action"


-- src:2600 | (b) where the justice is satisfied that the circumstances warrant such an action, order that the possession by that person of any weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance, or of any such thing, be prohibited during any period, not exceeding five years, that is specified in the order, beginning on the making of the order.
@ref s 117.05(4)(b) (src:2600)
GIVEN period IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(4)(b) the period of the order is not more than five years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF period's years TIMES 12 PLUS period's months LESS THAN 60 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF period's years TIMES 12 PLUS period's months EQUALS 60 AND period's days EQUALS 0 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the period, not exceeding five years"

@ref s 117.05(4)(b) (src:2600)
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(4)(b) the order begins on the day on which it is made` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the period begins` EQUALS `the day on which the order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "beginning on the day on which the order is made"

-- src:2602 | (5) Where a justice does not make an order under subsection (4), or where a justice does make such an order but does not prohibit the possession of all of the things referred to in that subsection, the justice shall include in the record a statement of the justice’s reasons.
@ref s 117.05(5) (src:2602)
GIVEN `the justice does not make an order under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice makes an order but does not prohibit the possession of all of the things referred to in that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(5) the justice is bound to include a statement of reasons in the record` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the justice does not make an order under subsection (4)` OR `the justice makes an order but does not prohibit the possession of all of the things referred to in that subsection`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a justice does not make an order under subsection (4)"


-- src:2604 | (6) Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (4).
@ref s 117.05(6) (src:2604)
GIVEN `the order is made under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(6) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under subsection (4)` AND `the provision`'s `section` AT LEAST 113 AND `the provision`'s `section` AT MOST 117
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (4)"

-- src:2606 | (7) Where a justice makes an order under subsection (4) in respect of a person, or in respect of any thing that was seized from a person, the person may appeal to the superior court against the order.
@ref s 117.05(7) (src:2606)
GIVEN `the appellant is the person in respect of whom the order is made, or from whom the thing was seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice makes an order under subsection (4) in respect of a person, or in respect of any thing that was seized from a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(7) the person may appeal to the superior court against the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the justice makes an order under subsection (4) in respect of a person, or in respect of any thing that was seized from a person`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a justice makes an order under subsection (4) in respect of a person, or in respect of any thing that was seized from a person"
        IF `the appellant is the person in respect of whom the order is made, or from whom the thing was seized` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2608 | (8) Where a justice does not make a finding as described in subsection (4) following the hearing of an application under subsection (1), or makes the finding but does not make an order to the effect described in paragraph (4)(b), the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the failure to make the finding or to make an order to the effect so described.
@ref s 117.05(8) (src:2608)
GIVEN `the justice does not make a finding as described in subsection (4) following the hearing of an application under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice makes the finding but does not make an order to the effect described in paragraph (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant is the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(8) the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the failure to make the finding or the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the justice does not make a finding as described in subsection (4) following the hearing of an application under subsection (1)` OR `the justice makes the finding but does not make an order to the effect described in paragraph (4)(b)`) AND `the appellant is the Attorney General` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a justice does not make a finding as described in subsection (4)"


-- src:2610 | (9) The provisions of Part XXVII, except sections 785 to 812, 816 to 819 and 829 to 838, apply in respect of an appeal made under subsection (7) or (8) with such modifications as the circumstances require and as if each reference in that Part to the appeal court were a reference to the superior court.
@ref s 117.05(9) (src:2610)
GIVEN `the section of Part XXVII in question` IS A NUMBER
      `the provision is a provision of Part XXVII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is made under subsection (7) or (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.05(9) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the section of Part XXVII in question` AT LEAST 785 AND `the section of Part XXVII in question` AT MOST 812) OR (`the section of Part XXVII in question` AT LEAST 816 AND `the section of Part XXVII in question` AT MOST 819) OR (`the section of Part XXVII in question` AT LEAST 829 AND `the section of Part XXVII in question` AT MOST 838) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except sections 785 to 812, 816 to 819 and 829 to 838"
        IF `the provision is a provision of Part XXVII` AND `the appeal is made under subsection (7) or (8)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only an appeal made under subsection (7) or (8) is reached

§§ `s 117.06 Where no finding or application`


-- src:2613 | (a) no application is made under subsection 117.05(1) within thirty days after the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant, as the case may be; or
@ref s 117.06(1)(a) (src:2613)
GIVEN `the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the position is checked` IS A DATE
      `an application was made under subsection 117.05(1) within the thirty days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.06(1)(a) no application was made within thirty days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an application was made under subsection 117.05(1) within the thirty days` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no application is made under subsection 117.05(1) within thirty days"
        IF `the date on which the position is checked` AT MOST `the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant` PLUS 30 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the thirty days have not yet run
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2612 | 117.06 (1) Any thing or document seized pursuant to subsection 117.04(1) or (2) shall be returned to the person from whom it was seized if
-- src:2613 | (a) no application is made under subsection 117.05(1) within thirty days after the date of execution of the warrant or of the seizure without a warrant, as the case may be; or
-- src:2614 | (b) an application is made under subsection 117.05(1) within the period referred to in paragraph (a), and the justice does not make a finding as described in subsection 117.05(4).
@ref s 117.06(1) (src:2612-2614)
GIVEN `the thing or document was seized pursuant to subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.06(1)(a) no application was made within thirty days` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an application is made under subsection 117.05(1) within the period referred to in paragraph (a), and the justice does not make a finding as described in subsection 117.05(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.06(1) the thing or document is to be returned to the person from whom it was seized` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing or document was seized pursuant to subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` AND ((`the answer of s 117.06(1)(a) no application was made within thirty days` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `an application is made under subsection 117.05(1) within the period referred to in paragraph (a), and the justice does not make a finding as described in subsection 117.05(4)`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be returned to the person from whom it was seized if"

-- src:2616 | (2) Where, pursuant to subsection (1), any thing is returned to the person from whom it was seized and an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate, as the case may be, is revoked pursuant to subsection 117.04(4), the justice referred to in paragraph (1)(b) may order that the revocation be reversed and that the authorization, licence or registration certificate be restored.
@ref s 117.06(2) (src:2616)
GIVEN `the thing is returned to the person from whom it was seized pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate is revoked pursuant to subsection 117.04(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the justice referred to in paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.06(2) the justice may order that the revocation be reversed and the authorization, licence or registration certificate restored` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is returned to the person from whom it was seized pursuant to subsection (1)` AND `an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate is revoked pursuant to subsection 117.04(4)` AND `the person is the justice referred to in paragraph (1)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, pursuant to subsection (1), any thing is returned"
